\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces System architecture of the MMSAR evaluation framework. Visible RGB and thermal infrared video streams are synthesized from text prompts, followed by cross-modality thermal transfer, dual-crop ($640 \times 640$) spatial extraction, video-level annotation in Label Studio, and 24~Hz frame extraction. Curated sequences are partitioned into 240-frame episodes under a parent-video grouped split protocol ([TBD]) with anti-adjacency snippet shuffling to eliminate cross-tile spatial leakage. At edge inference, parallel lightweight YOLO11n detectors process incoming RGB and thermal frames at 24~Hz ($T_s \approx 41.7$~ms), integrated via soft disjunctive late fusion ($s[n] = \max (c_{\text  {RGB}}[n], c_{\text  {Thermal}}[n])$) and evaluated across five lightweight temporal decision methods ($W = 5$ frames, 208~ms latency bound).}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system_architecture}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
